/-
# The Hanna Neumann Conjecture (Bestvina, Questions in Geometric Group Theory, Q 3.1)

M. Bestvina, Questions in Geometric Group Theory, Q 3.1 (Hanna Neumann Conjecture): if `A` and `B`
are nontrivial subgroups of a free group, then `rk(A ∩ B) - 1 ≤ (rk(A) - 1)(rk(B) - 1)`.
-/

module

public import Batteries.Util.ProofWanted
public import Mathlib.GroupTheory.Rank

@[expose] public section

namespace MathlibExt.GroupTheory.HannaNeumannConjectureAMR10Problem0301Wanted

/-!
Source: M. Bestvina, Questions in Geometric Group Theory (updated July 2004), Q 3.1 (Hanna Neumann
Conjecture), https://www.math.utah.edu/~bestvina/eprints/questions-updated.pdf. UnsolvedMath record
UM-01100301 (`AMR-010-0301`), dataset ulamai/UnsolvedMath v1.8.0.

The conjecture concerns finitely generated subgroups (as in Hanna Neumann's original statement and
in Friedman's and Mineyev's theorems); the source's `rk` is the minimal number of generators,
Mathlib's `Group.rank` of the subgroup as a group, which needs a `Group.FG` instance. `A ∩ B` is
finitely generated by Howson's theorem, so the instance argument `Group.FG ↥(A ⊓ B)` is always
available and loses nothing. The free group `FreeGroup α` has an arbitrary basis type `α`; the
inequality is stated in `ℤ`, so `rk(A ∩ B) = 0` (trivial intersection) gives `-1` on the left.
-/

/-- The Hanna Neumann Conjecture (Bestvina, Q 3.1): if `A` and `B` are nontrivial finitely generated
subgroups of a free group, then `rk(A ∩ B) - 1 ≤ (rk(A) - 1)(rk(B) - 1)`, where `rk` is Mathlib's
`Group.rank` (the least size of a generating set); `A ∩ B` is finitely generated by Howson's
theorem, so the instance `Group.FG ↥(A ⊓ B)` always holds. -/
def hannaNeumannInequality : Prop :=
  ∀ (α : Type) (A B : Subgroup (FreeGroup α)) [Group.FG A] [Group.FG B] [Group.FG ↥(A ⊓ B)],
    A ≠ ⊥ → B ≠ ⊥ →
      (Group.rank ↥(A ⊓ B) : ℤ) - 1 ≤ ((Group.rank A : ℤ) - 1) * ((Group.rank B : ℤ) - 1)

/--
Resolved true: Friedman (and independently Mineyev) proved the Hanna Neumann Conjecture, even in its
strengthened form: for nontrivial finitely generated subgroups `A`, `B` of a free group, `rank(A ∩
B) - 1 ≤ (rank A - 1)(rank B - 1)`. Source: M. Bestvina, Questions in Geometric Group Theory
(updated July 2004), Q 3.1 (Hanna Neumann Conjecture),
https://www.math.utah.edu/~bestvina/eprints/questions-updated.pdf; resolution: J. Friedman, Sheaves
on graphs, their homological invariants, and a proof of the Hanna Neumann conjecture, Mem. Amer.
Math. Soc. 233 (2015), no. 1100, arXiv:1105.0129; I. Mineyev, Submultiplicativity and the Hanna
Neumann conjecture, Ann. of Math. 175 (2012), 393-414, Friedman, Chapter 2 (The Hanna Neumann
Conjecture), Theorem 2.1: "The Hanna Neumann Conjecture and the Strengthened Hanna Neumann
Conjecture hold", the conjecture being rank(H ∩ K) - 1 ≤ (rank(H) - 1)(rank(K) - 1) for nontrivial
finitely generated subgroups H, K of a free group, https://arxiv.org/abs/1105.0129.
-/
public theorem_wanted hannaNeumannInequality_holds : hannaNeumannInequality

end MathlibExt.GroupTheory.HannaNeumannConjectureAMR10Problem0301Wanted
